 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A balanced diet contains all the food classes in the right amounts: carbohydrates (energy), proteins (growth and repair), fats (energy, warmth), vitamins and mineral salts (protection), fibre (roughage, against constipation) and water.\nHealthy habits:\n• eat three regular meals and never skip breakfast;\n• eat fruit and vegetables every day;\n• choose whole grains (brown rice, whole maize) and beans;\n• limit sugar, salt, fried and fatty foods and sweet drinks;\n• drink plenty of clean water;\n• do not overeat; eat slowly;\n• wash hands before eating;\n• eat local foods that are fresh and cheap: ndolé, beans, plantain, eru, fish, fruits in season.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "m": "rice and fried plantain only"
  },
  "problem": "A pupil's lunch is {m}. Is it balanced? How can it be improved?",
  "steps": [
   "Rice and plantain are mostly carbohydrate; frying adds fat.",
   "There is no protein and few vitamins or fibre."
  ],
  "answer": "Not balanced: add beans or fish (protein) and vegetables or fruit (vitamins, fibre).",
  "checks": []
